<title>USA: Conceptronic to sue Vitronics.</title>
<headline>Conceptronic to sue Vitronics.</headline>
<dateline>PORTSMOUTH, N.H. 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Conceptronics Inc said on  Monday it named Vitronics Corp and Vitronics Chairman and Chief Executive Officer James Manfield in a lawsuit, citing malicious prosecution and abuse of the legal process.</p>
<p>The suit claims Vitronics, when it began a 1991 patent infringement case against Conceptronics, knew or should have known that the suit was without merit, Conceptronics said.</p>
<p>Conceptronics said the Patent and Trademark Office rejected a key claim of the patent and jury verdict in 1995 gave a unanimous non-infringement verdit.</p>
<p>The company said it was suing for no less than $1.3 million, with additional amounts to be determined.</p>
<p>Conceptronics makes computer controlled capital equipment.</p>
</text>
